    "Grid of rectangular element cells, 18 columns x 7 rows, with the characteristic periodic-table gaps (period 1 has only group 1 and group 18; periods 2-3 skip groups 3-12)",
    "Group 1 cells shaded light purple with labels Li+, Na+, K+, Rb+, Cs+, Fr+ (period-1 group-1 cell shaded pale gray with no label)",
    "Group 2 cells shaded light green with labels Be2+, Mg2+, Ca2+, Sr2+, Ba2+, Ra2+",
    "Transition-metal d-block cells shaded pale tan; labeled cells Cr3+/Cr6+, Mn2+, Fe2+/Fe3+, Co2+, Ni2+, Cu+/Cu2+, Zn2+, Ag+, Cd2+, Pt2+, Au+/Au3+, Hg2^2+/Hg2+; remaining d-block cells tan but unlabeled",
    "Group 13-14 cells mostly white/unshaded with labels Al3+ (period 3, group 13) and C4- (period 2, group 14)",
    "Group 15-16 nonmetal cells shaded pink/salmon with labels N3-, O2-, P3-, S2-, As3-, Se2-, Te2-",
    "Group 17 halogen cells shaded pale lavender-blue with labels F-, Cl-, Br-, I-, At-",
    "Group 18 noble-gas cells shaded cyan with labels He, Ne, Ar, Kr, Xe, Rn and no charge",
    "Red rectangular outline around the period-6 and period-7 group-3 cells with a red curved arrow pointing down-right to the detached f-block",
