  "reconstructionNotes": "Recreate the classic 18-column x 7-row periodic table outline with the standard gaps, drawn as rounded-corner rectangular cells with thin gray borders and a small gap between cells. Left edge: purple 'Period' label rotated vertically plus purple period numbers 1-7. Top: blue 'Group' label and blue group numbers positioned above their columns (3-12 sit lower, aligned above the period-4 row where the d-block begins). Title in bold black, centered above the table. Fill colors: group 1 light purple/lavender, group 2 pale green, d-block pale tan/cream, groups 15-16 nonmetals dusty pink, group 17 pale blue-lavender, group 18 cyan, unlabeled p-block metals white. Cell text is bold black element symbol with superscript charge (e.g. Li with superscript +, Fe2+ over Fe3+ stacked on two lines where two charges are shown). Below and right of the main table, draw the detached f-block as two 14-cell rows with heavy gray borders, top row pale green marked '*', bottom row pale pink marked '**', connected to the group-3 cells of periods 6-7 by a red rectangle outline and a red curved arrow. For interactivity: clicking a cell draws a thick dark outline on it and populates a side/below info panel; the group slider draws a translucent yellow-gold vertical band over the selected column (spanning all populated cells) with a caption naming the typical charge; the color toggle re-fills every cell using a diverging charge scale (blues for positive, reds for negative, gray for zero, hatched/mottled tan for variable) with the legend swapping accordingly."
}

